==English==

===Etymology===
From {{term|caterwrawe|lang=enm}} (one of numerous earlier variants); from {{term|cater||cat|lang=enm}} + {{term|wrawen|lang=enm}}/{{term|wrawlen||cry like a cat|lang=enm}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈkæt.ə.wɔːl/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈkæt.ɚ.wɑːl/}}
* {{audio|en-us-caterwaul.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Verb===
{{WikiSaurus-link|argument}}
{{en-verb}}

# {{intransitive}} To [[cry]] as cats in [[rut]]ting time; to make a [[harsh]], [[offensive]] [[noise]].
# To have a [[noisy]] [[argument]], like cats.

